  "body": "A High Fidelity Photo trace of a 2048 \u00d7 2048 photo made 733,000 paths and 7.8 million anchors; the selected result's outlines and anchor squares then built a 1.8 GB egui mesh, over wgpu's largest buffer, and the app quit painting it (after reaching 6.4 GB of memory).\n\n- **Canvas** (`crates/ui-egui/src/canvas.rs`): a selection with more than 100,000 anchors shows its bounds instead of every outline and anchor square; the hover highlight skips such an object. The Contextual Task Bar and that outline read the selection's bounds from a per-revision cache (`VectorcraftApp::selection_bounds`), so a selected trace draws a frame in ~20 ms instead of ~170 ms.\n- **Image Trace** (`crates/trace`): colour layers are traced in parallel with scoped threads (26 s \u2192 1.9 s for that photo; the web build traces them in turn). The new `trace_within` stops once the paths pass an anchor budget; `imageTrace.make` allows 2,000,000 and otherwise fails with \"this trace would make more than \u2026 anchor points \u2026 raise Noise, lower Paths or Colors, or pick a lower-fidelity preset\". Images over 64 megapixels are refused from their header, before decoding.\n- The trace crate's messages are now in the i18n message scan, with es and it rows.\n- Tests: an anchor budget refuses the trace and the full budget equals `trace`; parallel layers keep their order across runs; an oversized PNG header is refused before decoding; a selection past the overlay budget draws its bounds while a normal path still draws its outline and anchors.\n- ROADMAP: Image Trace bullet and Last updated.\n\nTried live in the desktop app with a synthetic 2048\u00b2 photo: High Fidelity Photo now reports the error in the status bar; Low Fidelity Photo (144k paths, 1.1M anchors) traces, selects, moves and hovers without crashing at ~950 MB.\n\nNot covered: Image Trace still runs on the UI thread (a long trace blocks the window while it runs), and the tracer's edge quality is unchanged.\n\n## Checks\n- Rebased on origin/main 843f4610.\n- `cargo test -p vectorcraft-trace -p vectorcraft-engine -p vectorcraft-ui-egui`, `cargo clippy -p vectorcraft-trace -p vectorcraft-engine -p vectorcraft-ui-egui --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo xtask wasm`, i18n tests.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
